---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Orkha';
const description =
  'How Orkha collects, uses, and protects personal information under the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173).';

// Displayed as the policy effective date. Update if the policy changes.
const effective = 'July 2026';
const a = BUSINESS.address;
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/privacy/">
  <section class="container-x py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-prose" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-ink-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-500">Effective date: {effective}</p>

      <div class="prose-body mt-8 space-y-8 text-ink-700">
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          {BUSINESS.legalName} (“Orkha”, “we”, “us”, or “our”) respects your privacy and is committed
          to protecting your personal data. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use,
          disclose, and safeguard your information in accordance with Republic Act No. 10173, the
          <strong> Data Privacy Act of 2012</strong> of the Philippines, its Implementing Rules and
          Regulations, and the issuances of the National Privacy Commission (NPC).
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">1. Information we collect</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">We may collect the following personal information when you interact with our website or services:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>Contact details you provide through our forms — such as your name, email address, phone number, and business name.</li>
            <li>The content of inquiries and messages you send us, including through our website form and connected social media channels.</li>
            <li>Basic technical information automatically collected by our hosting provider, such as your browser type and approximate location, for security and performance.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            Our contact form is provided through a third-party form service (LeadConnector /
            GoHighLevel). Information you submit through that form is processed by that provider on our
            behalf.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">2. How we use your information</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">We process your personal data only for legitimate business purposes, including to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>Respond to your inquiries and communicate with you about our services.</li>
            <li>Prepare proposals and provide the services you request.</li>
            <li>Maintain records of our correspondence and business relationship.</li>
            <li>Improve our website and comply with legal obligations.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">3. Legal basis for processing</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            We process your personal data on the basis of your consent (which you give when you
            voluntarily submit an inquiry), the necessity of processing to take steps at your request
            before entering into a contract, and our legitimate interests in operating and improving
            our business — always balanced against your rights and freedoms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">4. Sharing and disclosure</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            We do not sell your personal information. We may share it with trusted third-party service
            providers who help us operate our website and communications (for example, our form and
            hosting providers), only to the extent necessary and subject to appropriate safeguards. We
            may also disclose information where required by law or by a lawful order of a competent
            authority.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">5. Data retention</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes described in
            this policy, to comply with our legal, tax, and accounting obligations, or to resolve
            disputes. When no longer needed, information is securely deleted or anonymised.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">6. Your rights as a data subject</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">Under the Data Privacy Act of 2012, you have the right to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li>Be informed about how your personal data is processed.</li>
            <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
            <li>Object to or withdraw consent to processing.</li>
            <li>Rectify inaccurate or outdated information.</li>
            <li>Erase or block your data under the conditions allowed by law.</li>
            <li>Data portability, where applicable.</li>
            <li>Be indemnified for damages arising from unlawful processing.</li>
            <li>Lodge a complaint with the National Privacy Commission.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">7. Data security</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            We implement reasonable organisational, physical, and technical measures to protect your
            personal data against unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. No
            method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, however, and we cannot
            guarantee absolute security.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">8. Cookies</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            Our website is built to be lightweight and does not use advertising or tracking cookies.
            Third-party embedded services (such as our contact form) may set their own cookies
            necessary for their functionality.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">9. Contact us</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            To exercise any of your rights or to ask a question about this policy, contact us at:
          </p>
          <address class="mt-3 not-italic leading-relaxed">
            {BUSINESS.legalName}<br />
            {a.street}, {a.barangay}, {a.city}, {a.region}, {a.country}<br />
            Email: <a class="link-underline" href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a><br />
            Phone: <a class="link-underline" href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneHref}`}>{BUSINESS.phoneDisplay}</a>
          </address>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            If you believe your data privacy rights have been violated, you may also file a complaint
            with the National Privacy Commission (privacy.gov.ph).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900">10. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this
            page with a revised effective date.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
